From: Sebastian Buergel <SCBuergel@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:22:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(pix): let the embedder route the Curvy relayer's traffic
 at run time

A VPN client's exit holds a session's return traffic back once the session's free
allowance is used up and no deposit is visible yet. A deposit that has to reach the
Curvy relayer through that same session can then no longer be made.

RelayerRoute is a switch the embedder gets on ReactorHandle. Pointing it at a local
listener (for example a separate HOPR session to the relayer) sends the pool's relayer
connections there; TLS still runs end to end with the relayer. Setting the route opens
the first connection in the background. While no route is set nothing changes.

Uses CurvyDepositPool::with_http_client from hopr-strategy 9.2.0.

